            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0129" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4062/11–12.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Francis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department has received your No. 225 of
                    the 8th of May last, relative to the expulsion case of Mr. Selig Fink, and
                    awaits the reply of the foreign office to your note of May 7 last on this case
                    and on the general question involved of former Austrian or Hungarian subjects
                    returning as American citizens to the country of their origin.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
